731 0 obj
<</Title(Most conversations about climate change happen at a scale that feels far from ordinary life „ treaties, policy, corporate targets. But the actual damage, and the actual fixing, both happen locally: a littered park, a filthy riverside, an old age home nobody visits, a hungry stray. As an engineering student trained to think in systems, this internship pushed me the other way „ toward individuals and neighbourhoods.)/Dest[ 13 0 R /Fit]/Parent 720 0 R >>
endobj
732 0 obj
<</Title(Climate change hits vulnerable groups hardest „ children without clean surroundings or supplies, elderly citizens rarely included in the conversation, and animals with no voice at all. Working alone meant every call, every bag carried, every conversation was mine to manage „ slower and harder, but it made the experience genuinely mine.)/Dest[ 13 0 R /Fit]/Parent 721 0 R /Next 733 0 R >>
endobj
